==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3.33~13.33 seconds<sup>100f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3.33~13.33 seconds<sup>100f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 8~20 seconds<sup>240f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Mooth]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 33.33~53.33 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[The Face]] spawns as the boss.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Rain D.]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Rain D.]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**1 [[Rain D.]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Concentrate on using range attackers such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] to constantly knockback the [[Rain D.]] and along with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall]] and [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cat]] of course to stall them. You also want to concentrate on killing [[Mooth]] purely for income, as spawning [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] will greatly help on moving your team up.

Throughout the battle you will always want to keep spawning Dragon Cat and your stallers, as when you hit the enemy base, Rain D's will constantly come out. [[The Face]] should not be a problem at all in this battle if you protect your ranged cats well.

